This is a miscompilation bug in InstCombine.
Issue title: [clang] Miscompile with -O3 and -O0/1/2 since 18.1.0
Detailed information:
BUG TYPE:
    miscompilation

VERIFICATION RESULT:
    Invalid refinement in @wrong_gep_arg_into_phi -- Source is more defined than target

VIOLATED PROPERTY:
    UB refinement

SOURCE (pre-transformation IR):
target datalayout = "e-p:64:64:64-i1:8:8-i8:8:8-i16:16:16-i32:32:32-i64:64:64-f32:32:32-f64:64:64-v64:64:64-v128:128:128-a0:0:64-s0:64:64-f80:128:128-n8:16:32:64"

define i64 @wrong_gep_arg_into_phi(ptr noundef %ptr) {
entry:
  %add.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %ptr, i64 1
  br label %for.cond

for.cond:                                         ; preds = %for.cond, %entry
  %.pn = phi ptr [ %add.ptr, %entry ], [ %incdec.ptr, %for.cond ]
  %val = load i8, ptr %.pn, align 1
  %cond = icmp ne i8 %val, 0
  %incdec.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %.pn, i64 1
  br i1 %cond, label %for.cond, label %exit

exit:                                             ; preds = %for.cond
  ret i64 0
}

TARGET (post-transformation IR):
; ModuleID = '<stdin>'
source_filename = "<stdin>"
target datalayout = "e-p:64:64:64-i1:8:8-i8:8:8-i16:16:16-i32:32:32-i64:64:64-f32:32:32-f64:64:64-v64:64:64-v128:128:128-a0:0:64-s0:64:64-f80:128:128-n8:16:32:64"

define i64 @wrong_gep_arg_into_phi(ptr noundef %ptr) {
entry:
  br label %for.cond

for.cond:                                         ; preds = %for.cond, %entry
  %ptr.pn = phi ptr [ %ptr, %entry ], [ %.pn, %for.cond ]
  %.pn = getelementptr inbounds i8, ptr %ptr.pn, i64 1
  %val = load i8, ptr %.pn, align 1
  %cond.not = icmp eq i8 %val, 0
  br i1 %cond.not, label %exit, label %for.cond

exit:                                             ; preds = %for.cond
  ret i64 0
}

WHAT THE TRANSFORMATION CHANGED:
  modified:
    %.pn
      source: %.pn = phi ptr [ %add.ptr, %entry ], [ %incdec.ptr, %for.cond ]
      target: %.pn = getelementptr inbounds i8, ptr %ptr.pn, i64 1
  only in target:
    %ptr.pn: %ptr.pn = phi ptr [ %ptr, %entry ], [ %.pn, %for.cond ]
    %cond.not: %cond.not = icmp eq i8 %val, 0
  only in source:
    %add.ptr: %add.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %ptr, i64 1
    %cond: %cond = icmp ne i8 %val, 0
    %incdec.ptr: %incdec.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %.pn, i64 1

CRITICAL VALUES:
    %.pn
    %add.ptr
    %cond
    %incdec.ptr
    %ptr.pn
    %val

DEPENDENCY CHAIN (source):
    %add.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %ptr, i64 1
    %.pn = phi ptr [ %add.ptr, %entry ], [ %incdec.ptr, %for.cond ]
    %val = load i8, ptr %.pn, align 1
    %cond = icmp ne i8 %val, 0
    %incdec.ptr = getelementptr i8, ptr %.pn, i64 1

CONTROL FLOW (blocks entered by the failing execution):
    %for.cond
    %exit

COUNTEREXAMPLE INPUT:
    ptr noundef %ptr = pointer(non-local, block_id=1, offset=-1) / Address=#x00

DIVERGENCE (source vs target on that input):
    %ptr.pn: source = (not computed)   target = pointer(non-local, block_id=1, offset=-1) / Address=#x00
    %.pn: source = pointer(non-local, block_id=1, offset=0) / Address=#x01   target = poison
    %val: source = #x00 (0)   target = UB triggered!

MEMORY STATE:
  source:
===================
NON-LOCAL BLOCKS:
Block 0 >	size: 0	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: false	address: 0
Block 1 >	size: 4	align: 1	alloc type: 0	alive: true	address: 1
Contents:
*: #x00

INTERPRETATION:
    A transformation may not introduce undefined behaviour. Any execution that is UB-free in the source must remain UB-free in the target.
    The earliest reported divergence is at %ptr.pn.
    The target attaches 'inbounds' to %.pn, which the source does not. If that guarantee is not implied by the source, attaching it is unsound on its own.

